The file named <key>.txt is an IndexNow key. IndexNow is how Bing, Yandex,
Seznam and Naver are told a URL changed instead of being left to discover
it on their own schedule; the key file is what proves the submission came
from whoever controls this host.

The key is not a secret — it is meant to be publicly readable at
https://mastmq.github.io/<key>.txt, and the protocol does not work if it
is not. Deleting it silently invalidates every future submission.

Google does not participate. It deprecated sitemap ping in 2023 and takes
submissions only through Search Console.
